#N canvas 30 30 2700 2200 12;
#X text 20 20 u_state -- THE DATA STORE \, and the only file that says WHEN state is written. It owns two u_store instances and the state bus. It knows nothing about what any key MEANS: a contributor names its own key and declares its own policy \, so an abstraction written long after this one persists itself with no change here. That is the whole point of the phase., f 58;
#X text 900 20 creation arg 1: the data DIRECTORY \, absolute and with no trailing slash. inlet 1: a bang meaning RESTORE NOW \, wired from u_init because startup ORDER is u_init's. outlets: none -- everything leaves on the state bus., f 58;
#X text 1560 20 THE BUS \, and it is one name with disjoint selectors so there is no loop. A contributor sends put auto KEY ... or answers a save broadcast with put manual KEY ... \; u_state sends save when a commit is asked for and restore KEY ... at load. Contributors route save and restore \; this file routes put and rejects its own traffic into nothing., f 58;
#X text 20 180 A MANUAL ANSWER MUST BE SYNCHRONOUS \, and this is the one rule a contributor can break invisibly. Pd is eager \, synchronous and depth-first \, so by the time the save broadcast RETURNS every answer is already stored -- which is why the write below sits on the LEFT outlet of the trigger and needs no settle timer at all. A contributor that answers from behind a del is simply not in the file \, and the failure is a short file rather than an error. Say so in the contributor \, not just here., f 90;
